  "notes": "The whole upstream test registers a delivery callback for an integer sender. It checks delivery for the original literal and an equal integer constructed at runtime. PR 144 made the second delivery fail. PR 148 restores integer matching by value in the exact one-file historical repair. The reference tests the integer behavior. The repair also restores value-based matching for strings. Across seeds 11, 23, and 37 the reference passes on the parent, fails its second assertion on the introducing merge, and passes on the controlled repair. Each bad call reaches introduced lines 42, 45, 49, and 52 in src/blinker/_utilities.py. All native pytest tests pass 30, 26, and 26 respectively. The separate repeat uses the same structured reporting and matches every node ID. Its summary SHA-256 is 9e808271e09de0af4a1879e96413fe31d6aaed0de43c61b887b3e61985b5be29. PR descriptions are omitted. Exact observed PR timestamps and merge associations are retained."
